WEBVTT

00:01.020 --> 00:04.960
Everyone has a public and a private face.

00:04.960 --> 00:07.490
Some hide one side of 
themselves deliberately.

00:07.490 --> 00:09.720
Others, not so much.

00:10.370 --> 00:14.610
Some people's designs change 
every time you flip them over,

00:15.220 --> 00:18.370
and occasionally you meet someone

00:18.640 --> 00:23.790
whose front and back are both jokers.

00:24.330 --> 00:25.990
Cards like that

00:25.990 --> 00:29.510
have a strange tendency 
to gather in one place.

02:03.740 --> 02:05.720
Hold still.

02:07.040 --> 02:09.160
S-Sure. Thanks.

02:09.520 --> 02:10.450
Hey,

02:10.450 --> 02:13.120
are you really from a 
group called the Heilei?

02:14.730 --> 02:17.190
I have questions for you, too,

02:19.590 --> 02:20.980
but talk can wait.

02:29.930 --> 02:32.210
Those are your fingers stretching, right?

02:35.640 --> 02:39.180
Know your limits, kid. Your legs are shaking.

02:40.570 --> 02:44.390
By the way... tell me. What 
happened to your arms and legs?

02:44.700 --> 02:52.350
Last I checked, your severed limbs were 
still in my eldest sister's collection.

02:52.690 --> 02:57.310
Well, I don't know if you 
want a rematch with her,

02:57.310 --> 03:00.320
but we've already seen 
through your Heilei tricks.

03:01.530 --> 03:03.280
Don't get the wrong idea.

03:03.820 --> 03:05.580
I'm not a Heilei anymore.

03:06.460 --> 03:09.460
Do you think I'm shaking because I'm scared?

03:09.810 --> 03:11.790
What, are you quivering with anticipation?

03:12.090 --> 03:13.310
Not quite.

03:14.220 --> 03:16.250
This is the growl of a savage beast!

03:32.140 --> 03:33.650
Now I get it!

03:35.360 --> 03:38.230
This is great! I'm having a blast!

03:38.710 --> 03:41.710
You really don't fight like a Heilei!

03:50.310 --> 03:51.290
But

03:51.290 --> 03:56.000
the way you use malice and misdirect 
opponents is still just like them.

03:59.710 --> 04:01.200
Bingo.

04:02.120 --> 04:03.840
So close.

04:05.390 --> 04:07.600
Missed by a hair.

04:07.600 --> 04:09.640
Targeting Higuro-san now

04:09.640 --> 04:12.100
is just what a Heilei would do.

04:12.490 --> 04:15.150
It looks like you couldn't quite escape

04:15.150 --> 04:17.520
your Heilei karma.

04:18.730 --> 04:19.610
Momoya-san!

04:19.850 --> 04:20.540
Huh?

04:28.030 --> 04:28.990
Misaki!

04:29.240 --> 04:30.710
Sakimiya-san.

04:32.420 --> 04:38.040
So you <i>are</i> one of us, 
Xiaoyu-kun! I kind of figured!

04:39.000 --> 04:41.210
P-Put me down!

04:42.670 --> 04:44.340
<i>What's going on?</i>

04:45.310 --> 04:47.800
<i>I know Momoya-san killed that girl.</i>

04:48.580 --> 04:51.390
<i>Is she "something beyond this world's laws"?</i>

04:52.330 --> 04:57.810
<i>I was told to report anything like that, 
separate from my current orders,</i>

04:57.810 --> 05:01.280
<i>but I never expected to 
actually see something.</i>

05:02.030 --> 05:03.690
<i>First, though...</i>

05:05.860 --> 05:09.450
<i>can I make it out of here alive?</i>

05:11.680 --> 05:13.170
Okay, okay.

05:13.170 --> 05:17.330
I get what's happening,
 even if I can't figure out how.

05:17.950 --> 05:22.460
The girl I know I killed is alive,
 and she got a power-up.

05:22.890 --> 05:25.920
How scary. How creepy.

05:26.230 --> 05:28.530
The world's going to hell.

05:28.530 --> 05:31.340
But more than that, it's fun.

05:31.340 --> 05:33.920
So, let's get started.

05:36.620 --> 05:38.690
We'll have so much fun

05:39.350 --> 05:41.900
playing our trump cards.

05:43.330 --> 05:45.500
Your long legs are gorgeous!

05:45.500 --> 05:47.360
And sexy, like a model's!

05:48.080 --> 05:50.120
Are you trying to seduce me?

05:50.750 --> 05:54.080
Oh, my big sisters are always 
saying the same thing.

05:54.730 --> 05:56.330
"You're a wimp,

05:56.330 --> 05:59.790
so use your looks as a distraction."

06:03.780 --> 06:04.800
<i>He's fast!</i>

06:05.210 --> 06:07.510
<i>No, he barely moved.</i>

06:21.890 --> 06:24.020
<i>Sakimiya-san can react to him.</i>

06:34.650 --> 06:36.380
Close call!

06:36.380 --> 06:38.290
I barely dodged that one.

06:38.590 --> 06:40.550
So, what's the plan, Xiaoyu-kun?

06:40.550 --> 06:41.250
Huh?!

06:41.250 --> 06:43.770
Wanna team up on him?

06:43.770 --> 06:47.630
Or are you the type who 
thinks one-on-one is cooler?

06:48.260 --> 06:50.130
I'm fine either way!

06:52.170 --> 06:54.990
How strange. How mysterious.

06:54.990 --> 06:58.810
I know I timed that slash 
perfectly to cut you.

07:00.050 --> 07:01.770
How do you explain that?

07:02.280 --> 07:04.060
<i>Something's been bugging me for a while.</i>

07:04.550 --> 07:08.000
<i>Sakimiya-san has no heartbeat.</i>

07:10.070 --> 07:11.490
So,

07:11.770 --> 07:15.660
Misaki-chan is a "vampire larva" right now?

07:15.940 --> 07:19.280
Yes. You could say she's almost a vampire.

07:19.280 --> 07:22.750
I used necromancy to alter the 
link between her body and soul,

07:22.750 --> 07:25.670
making her more like a vampire physically.

07:26.110 --> 07:31.970
So Misaki-chan's only new abilities 
now are heightened regeneration...

07:32.220 --> 07:33.170
Whoopsie!

07:33.170 --> 07:35.220
...and turning into a bat.

07:42.960 --> 07:44.190
<i>Damn him!</i>

07:45.900 --> 07:50.360
<i>He uses footwork with his long legs 
and his posture to mislead opponents.</i>

07:50.970 --> 07:53.240
<i>He really is using his 
"looks" as a distraction.</i>

07:53.240 --> 07:56.050
<i>Even the colors on his 
jacket must be calculated</i>

07:56.050 --> 07:59.830
<i>to make it seem like his 
arms and torso stretch!</i>

08:00.110 --> 08:01.560
Are you awake?

08:01.560 --> 08:04.170
I wonder what you'll show me next.

08:04.730 --> 08:05.660
Hmm?

08:05.660 --> 08:09.130
Well, you know that thing where 
it looks like your arms stretch?

08:09.130 --> 08:10.880
Mind if I copy it?

08:10.880 --> 08:13.970
Oh? Thinking of throwing your crowbar?

08:14.360 --> 08:16.430
I've got

08:16.640 --> 08:18.750
nothing up my sleeve!

08:22.470 --> 08:24.650
<i>What </i>is<i> that?</i>

08:24.650 --> 08:27.610
Come on! You could at least try to hide it!

08:31.010 --> 08:35.360
Too bad. I guess I couldn't 
split you in half.

08:35.860 --> 08:38.340
That wasn't centrifugal force from her throw.

08:38.340 --> 08:41.320
It consciously tore into me.

08:41.770 --> 08:46.250
You wouldn't happen to be Solitaire's 
apprentice, by any chance?

08:46.940 --> 08:49.870
Speaking of Misaki-chan, among other things,

08:49.870 --> 08:53.380
don't you think it's time you 
told Xiaoyu-kun what's going on?

08:53.690 --> 08:55.220
You have a point.

08:55.220 --> 08:58.150
When he gets back, I'll explain how things—

08:59.750 --> 09:01.950
Is something wrong, Hosorogi-san?

09:08.610 --> 09:11.360
I'd like to ask a small favor of you.

09:11.780 --> 09:15.820
The board we stand on is 
already awash in jokers.

09:15.820 --> 09:19.030
A hand full of jokers won't win any game.

09:19.030 --> 09:22.490
So, don't you think it's high time

09:22.700 --> 09:28.250
the players holding the cards 
looked up and studied each other?

09:31.690 --> 09:33.670
<b></b>Number Withheld
Incoming call

09:32.740 --> 09:33.670
What?

09:34.640 --> 09:35.730
Hello?

09:37.700 --> 09:39.720
<i>I'm surprised I reached you.</i>

09:40.050 --> 09:41.740
Who're you?

09:42.170 --> 09:44.430
<i>You're easily exploited.</i>

09:44.430 --> 09:48.280
<i>I told you to change phones 
and numbers regularly.</i>

09:49.820 --> 09:51.110
It can't be.

09:52.900 --> 09:55.690
Hosorogi...san?

10:02.330 --> 10:05.120
How are the Shinoyamas tied to that building?

10:05.120 --> 10:06.420
Let's see...

10:06.420 --> 10:09.040
The building's owner is Lisa Kuraki,

10:09.040 --> 10:12.010
granddaughter of industrialist Luis Kuraki.

10:12.010 --> 10:14.900
Her parents disappeared, 
and she inherited their assets.

10:14.900 --> 10:18.630
Then, while in high school, she got 
caught up in a kidnapping case.

10:18.630 --> 10:25.470
Wait. This kidnapping was solved by 
the cop who vanished in that building.

10:22.970 --> 10:25.930
<b>Inspector        Miyabi Hosorogi</b>

10:26.510 --> 10:27.570
Hosorogi-san?!

10:28.420 --> 10:30.410
Hosorogi-san, is it really you?!

10:30.410 --> 10:31.770
<i>Calm down.</i>

10:31.770 --> 10:36.070
<i>What kind of idiot goes around shouting 
my name? What if someone overhears you?</i>

10:43.530 --> 10:46.460
Anyway, are you the real deal?

10:46.460 --> 10:49.840
<i>Well, I've lost my ability 
to speak like most people.</i>

10:49.840 --> 10:53.020
<i>Or should I say it was taken from me?</i>

10:53.020 --> 10:55.960
Where are you now?! Can we meet in person?!

10:56.300 --> 11:01.300
<i>A smart guy like you should 
already realize that we can't.</i>

11:01.300 --> 11:05.280
Using the vocal cords of a dead pigeon found in an alley with its (ghost's) permission

11:01.300 --> 11:05.280
m 0 0 l 550 0 550 70 0 70


11:01.860 --> 11:07.090
<i>Of course, I can hardly expect you 
to understand my whole situation.</i>

11:07.420 --> 11:08.890
This looks... Wow.

11:09.340 --> 11:11.610
<i>You're right! I don't!</i>

11:11.610 --> 11:16.110
<i>The old you would never have gotten 
a high-school kid involved!</i>

11:16.110 --> 11:18.430
You mean Polka Shinoyama?

11:19.310 --> 11:21.440
The old me died.

11:21.440 --> 11:25.700
The current me is not the 
Miyabi Hosorogi you knew.

11:26.120 --> 11:29.040
<i>The awful part is that none of that is a lie.</i>

11:29.520 --> 11:33.250
That should give you an idea of 
the kind of enemies we've made.

11:34.640 --> 11:37.080
<i>I assume you still have that note?</i>

11:37.080 --> 11:37.710
Yeah.

11:37.940 --> 11:44.220
Don't be a prisoner of the past. 
At least choose the brand 
of your indulgences yourself. 
Corruption is eating away from the top. 
Don't trust anyone. 
There's another garage on
 the west side of that place.
 The signpost is inside.
 The key is behind the mirror of I-383.

11:37.940 --> 11:44.220
{blur3}m 0 0 l 265 0 265 210 0 210

11:38.270 --> 11:41.600
<i>I left numerous clues in it,</i>

11:41.600 --> 11:44.220
<i>but we can't afford to take our time anymore.</i>

11:44.530 --> 11:47.680
I'll tell you the bare minimum,

11:48.320 --> 11:51.170
since it seems like Clarissa is 
about to be dragged in again.

11:52.410 --> 11:54.800
If the enemy has started making moves again,

11:54.800 --> 11:57.590
we'll have to get ready to counter them.

11:57.590 --> 11:59.420
Clarissa, huh?

11:59.420 --> 12:01.540
She's a crook, too, you know?

12:01.540 --> 12:03.780
<i>That's beside the point.</i>

12:04.260 --> 12:06.060
<i>I won't ask you to agree.</i>

12:06.400 --> 12:09.330
<i>Let's save that discussion for another time.</i>

12:09.620 --> 12:11.290
Yeah, all right.

12:11.770 --> 12:14.000
We'll have a nice, long talk <i>later</i>.

12:14.610 --> 12:17.500
Now, what do I need to know?

12:18.000 --> 12:21.480
The final murder suspect 
I narrowed it down to—

12:21.860 --> 12:25.720
the mastermind at the heart of the 
infection in the police force—is...

12:29.590 --> 12:32.360
That's... not funny.

12:33.060 --> 12:34.490
So?

12:34.490 --> 12:38.770
Am I one of these "players"—
these masterminds you're talking about?

12:39.010 --> 12:44.240
As the head of the police,
 I'd say you're more than qualified.

12:44.990 --> 12:49.950
The superintendent general is 
merely one supervisor among many.

12:50.640 --> 12:54.700
The organization's head would 
be the National Police Agency,

12:54.700 --> 13:01.420
or, above it, the National Public Safety 
Commission and the prime minister.

13:01.420 --> 13:06.640
And given popular sovereignty, 
the PM answers to the citizens!

13:06.870 --> 13:09.930
No, that's not what I was trying to—

13:09.930 --> 13:14.680
In which case, each and every 
citizen is one of your "players"!

13:14.680 --> 13:16.390
<b>Indeed!</b>

13:15.170 --> 13:16.390
<i>Indeed.</i>

13:16.840 --> 13:22.100
Everyone is a player, a pawn, 
and a cog in the machine.

13:22.730 --> 13:28.320
Just like you used Prime Minister 
Kubikigawara as a pawn to show off.

13:29.080 --> 13:30.860
That takes me back.

13:30.860 --> 13:36.040
I never expected one snide remark 
to earn me such a lengthy lecture.

13:36.300 --> 13:40.120
Do you think you can baffle 
me by blowing smoke?

13:41.290 --> 13:45.190
So, you insist that I'm 
some kind of mastermind?

13:45.570 --> 13:50.260
Why show yourself to me, 
then? What are you after?

13:51.500 --> 13:53.420
Can't you tell?

13:53.420 --> 13:58.520
<i>No, you could never guess my plan,
 Mr. Superintendent General.</i>

13:58.520 --> 14:00.190
<i>Can you imagine</i>

14:00.710 --> 14:05.280
<i>that from here on out, 
I'm completely winging it?!</i>

14:05.540 --> 14:08.690
<i>An enigmatic entity ordered me killed.</i>

14:08.690 --> 14:13.990
<i>I guessed the mastermind was a big shot, 
so I went to rattle one, but...</i>

14:09.590 --> 14:13.990
<b>Better luck
next time</b>

14:14.970 --> 14:17.160
<b>Results So Far</b>

14:14.970 --> 14:17.160
<b>Got a talking-to</b>

14:15.530 --> 14:16.650
<i>What now?</i>

14:20.000 --> 14:21.960
Do you have any more plans?

14:22.340 --> 14:27.130
I don't think he'll fall for that... 
trick where you stretch your arm again.

14:28.330 --> 14:29.920
I bet not.

14:29.920 --> 14:32.260
That guy's good!

14:37.220 --> 14:38.340
Huh?

14:38.340 --> 14:40.480
But if I do that...

14:41.430 --> 14:43.630
Trust me, okay?

14:44.910 --> 14:46.780
Don't blame me if you die.

14:46.780 --> 14:49.320
Oh, wow! Are you worried about me?

14:49.320 --> 14:50.810
That's so nice!

14:51.990 --> 14:54.990
Are you done talking strategy?

14:55.220 --> 14:57.880
Yup! Thanks for waiting!

14:57.880 --> 14:59.620
No need for gratitude.

14:59.860 --> 15:02.290
I wanted some time myself.

15:02.290 --> 15:05.470
Time to think about your trick,

15:05.470 --> 15:07.940
and time to steel myself.

15:12.640 --> 15:14.780
<i>I knew it. Her clothes are cut.</i>

15:14.780 --> 15:16.810
<i>My blade </i>is<i> reaching her.</i>

15:16.810 --> 15:17.930
<i>In which case...</i>

15:38.390 --> 15:40.140
Caught you.

15:53.010 --> 15:54.760
Caught <i>you</i>.

15:55.510 --> 15:58.880
Am I dreaming?

15:59.620 --> 16:01.850
Well, who cares?

16:08.480 --> 16:10.160
They did it?!

16:10.160 --> 16:13.450
They beat an Agakura?! For real?!

16:13.750 --> 16:16.440
<i>We pulled it off, but...</i>

16:17.480 --> 16:19.860
<i>what just happened?</i>

16:20.360 --> 16:24.920
Once that guy grabs me, 
stab through my gut to get him.

16:25.970 --> 16:28.630
<i>It was too dark to see clearly,</i>

16:29.170 --> 16:34.250
<i>but Sakimiya-san looked and 
sounded like fluttering bats.</i>

16:34.570 --> 16:35.890
We did it!

16:37.850 --> 16:38.810
Ah!

16:38.810 --> 16:39.750
Watch out!

16:39.750 --> 16:40.770
Higuro's packing hea—

16:40.990 --> 16:44.230
Oh, that guy ran out on us.

16:44.230 --> 16:45.010
Huh?

16:45.560 --> 16:47.270
What?!

16:48.110 --> 16:50.230
Man. What a lifesaver.

16:50.470 --> 16:55.430
Trust Momoya-san to cut loose 
and draw everyone's attention.

16:55.430 --> 16:56.950
I'm truly grateful.

16:57.510 --> 17:02.410
If you beat those two,
I'd love to work with you again.

17:02.650 --> 17:05.950
If you lose, well... rest in peace.

17:06.450 --> 17:08.810
I won't waste your sacrifice.

17:10.410 --> 17:14.880
Now, I'd better report that I saw

17:14.880 --> 17:17.340
Metropolitan Police Department

17:15.350 --> 17:16.810
"something beyond this world's laws."

17:17.340 --> 17:19.300
<b><b>Number withheld</b></b>

17:17.340 --> 17:19.300
<b><b>Incoming call</b></b>

17:23.170 --> 17:24.740
Aren't you going to pick up?

17:24.740 --> 17:28.230
It's a personal call, and I'm on duty.

17:28.470 --> 17:29.870
I see.

17:31.720 --> 17:36.660
Is this another one of your warnings?
To suspect even old friends?

17:38.030 --> 17:40.420
Hopefully it will end up as a funny story.

17:40.420 --> 17:41.700
But you know, Tsubaki,

17:42.230 --> 17:45.660
<i>when you're in the police, everyone 
on the force is one of your own.</i>

17:46.230 --> 17:51.350
<i>Whether they're rural personnel you've 
never met or longtime partners,</i>

17:51.350 --> 17:55.590
<i>you can't afford to make a distinction 
once you start suspecting officers.</i>

17:56.720 --> 17:58.070
Now I'm sure.

17:59.070 --> 18:01.630
You're definitely still the same old you.

18:02.650 --> 18:05.890
Consider you dead? No can do.

18:05.890 --> 18:08.390
You're still alive inside us,

18:08.700 --> 18:12.400
so I won't let you bite the dust easy.

18:13.460 --> 18:14.600
<i>Suit yourself.</i>

18:14.600 --> 18:16.990
<i>It's time I hung up. I'll be in touch.</i>

18:17.260 --> 18:20.450
Oh, one more thing, Senpai.

18:21.090 --> 18:25.440
Did you ever consider that I might 
be a spy for your mastermind?

18:25.440 --> 18:27.660
<i>Have you forgotten what I'm like?</i>

18:28.040 --> 18:32.650
<i>If you are, I'll just shoot 
you between the eyes.</i>

18:32.650 --> 18:33.660
That figures.

18:34.480 --> 18:37.840
<b><b>Number Withheld
Incoming Call</b></b>

18:35.170 --> 18:37.840
Number withheld, so I can't call back.

18:38.060 --> 18:42.130
Should we trump up a warrant 
to have it disclosed?

18:42.130 --> 18:45.790
Don't even think about it. 
Any mole would catch on.

18:46.380 --> 18:47.850
That's a relief.

18:47.850 --> 18:49.810
You're still yourself, Inspector.

18:50.220 --> 18:51.340
Well, yeah.

18:51.340 --> 18:53.610
If anything, I've got my old edge ba—

18:54.770 --> 18:57.400
<b><b>Number Withheld
Incoming call</b></b>

18:55.480 --> 18:57.400
Again?

18:57.400 --> 18:59.310
Did Hosorogi-san forget to tell me—

18:59.860 --> 19:04.440
Question: I've just finished a job. Who am I?

19:04.440 --> 19:04.830
<i>Huh?</i>

19:05.130 --> 19:09.120
<i>Hint one: my name is Ten'a Sorimura.</i>

19:09.480 --> 19:10.540
Solitaire?!

19:10.540 --> 19:11.950
<i>Correct!</i>

19:11.950 --> 19:15.280
<i>I'm amazed you got it after only one hint.</i>

19:15.280 --> 19:17.920
<i>What intellect! What sagacity!</i>

19:17.920 --> 19:21.210
<i>As a prize, I'll tell you 
something interesting!</i>

19:21.210 --> 19:23.010
I don't have time for your games.

19:23.260 --> 19:28.840
<i>It's about the mastermind you just 
discussed with Inspector Hosorogi.</i>

19:28.840 --> 19:30.600
<i>Wouldn't you like to hear it?</i>

19:31.560 --> 19:36.800
<i>Act boldly now and then, and you'll 
gain things you didn't expect.</i>

19:36.800 --> 19:39.630
Just like I have.

19:41.180 --> 19:43.660
Sorry for the trouble.

19:44.030 --> 19:47.020
I didn't want to involve you 
any more than I had to,

19:47.020 --> 19:50.620
but if the police—if <i>they</i>—are here, 
I have no choice.

19:50.860 --> 19:56.340
That Iwanome guy must be over the 
moon now that he thinks you're alive.

19:57.090 --> 19:59.640
That was awfully cruel of you.

20:00.390 --> 20:02.170
Funny though it may sound, I agree.

20:02.170 --> 20:07.310
I always figured I'd meet a bad end.
 And then I actually did.

20:07.310 --> 20:14.270
Well, for now, I only hope Iwanome plays 
his cards as well as I think he will.

20:14.680 --> 20:18.970
Hosorogi-san was one thing, 
but now you're going to trust <i>Solitaire</i>?

20:18.970 --> 20:21.990
No, I don't believe a word he said.

20:22.330 --> 20:25.950
But as I've told you before, true or false—

20:25.950 --> 20:30.040
"Words people blurt out 
always mean something"?

20:30.490 --> 20:32.900
I'm just parroting Hosorogi-san, of course.

20:34.960 --> 20:38.670
<i>Come on. Pick up already.</i>

20:41.840 --> 20:43.670
Shouldn't you get that?

20:45.940 --> 20:47.630
Excuse me for a sec.

20:57.480 --> 20:59.900
Don't call me when I'm at work.

20:59.900 --> 21:01.440
I know I've told you that before.

21:01.650 --> 21:04.490
I have a top-priority report to make.

21:04.490 --> 21:06.160
It's the schoolgirl from that building.

21:06.630 --> 21:09.720
I know we killed her, 
but she came back to life.

21:10.230 --> 21:13.620
She's "something beyond this 
world's laws," as you put it.

21:14.200 --> 21:19.000
Also, I annoyed the Shinoyamas on 
this job, so I'll lie low for a bit.

21:19.550 --> 21:22.720
Can I ask you to keep me safe from them?

21:23.290 --> 21:24.800
Have no fear.

21:29.530 --> 21:34.390
Your position is secure 
under Sabaramond's aegis.

21:34.850 --> 21:36.880
You've done well, Higuro.

21:44.070 --> 21:45.950
<i>Wh-Why are you...?!</i>

21:46.660 --> 21:47.530
Are you nuts?!

21:47.530 --> 21:51.330
No way can I take a call from 
a reporter like you inside HQ!

21:51.330 --> 21:54.540
But I couldn't wait to tell you, Ran-nii!

21:54.540 --> 21:56.790
<b>Yatsu 
(eight ports)</b>

21:54.540 --> 21:56.790
<b>Eightport</b>

21:54.720 --> 21:56.790
<b>Real Name 
 </b>Kochou
 Yatsu

21:54.720 --> 21:56.790
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 190 0 190


21:57.330 --> 22:02.380
After Hosorogi-san died, one person rose 
through the ranks suspiciously fast!

22:02.980 --> 22:04.740
To be honest, I'm shocked.

22:05.150 --> 22:07.340
You saved me from getting the boot.

22:08.100 --> 22:11.640
I thought of you like family, 
and you stabbed me in the back.

22:12.790 --> 22:17.940
I screwed up recently, too, but saying your 
contact's name was beyond careless,

22:19.170 --> 22:20.500
Senior Commissioner Habaki!

22:25.380 --> 22:28.490
This guy's not moving. What should we do?

22:28.950 --> 22:31.050
We should steer clear of him.

22:32.310 --> 22:36.250
Still, it's over now... isn't it?

22:36.630 --> 22:38.690
Stop kidding around!

22:38.690 --> 22:40.790
Jeez! Why Habaki-san?!

22:40.790 --> 22:44.100
Listen, if you breathe a 
word of this to Iwa-san—

22:41.420 --> 22:48.650
That stream, where carp I caught.

22:50.390 --> 22:59.100
Even now, I dream of naught...

22:59.490 --> 23:07.640
...but my old country home.

23:07.090 --> 23:09.950
<b>Fire
Safety</b>

23:16.240 --> 23:20.270
<i>Your call cannot be completed 
because the number you have dialed</i>

23:19.620 --> 23:23.080
<b></b>Momoya
Calling

23:20.270 --> 23:23.540
<i>is not in service or is 
outside the service area.</i>

23:24.330 --> 23:27.170
Time for a scolding. Yes, a scolding.

23:27.820 --> 23:32.590
Oh, Momo-kun, how could you ignore an 
important call from your big sister?
